WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.134
-You guys, this is fun.

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.669
"Shark Week" is officially here.
-Yeah.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:04.870
[ Cheers ]

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.205
-And if you're excited
about that,

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.308
you're either a marine biologist
or really high.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.276
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.912
I read that "Shark Week" started
back in 1988.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.014
Yeah. It's been around
for over 30 years.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.216
Even crazier, they've just been
airing the same ten shows

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.752
and nobody's noticed.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.220
Get this, every year there are

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.556
about 80 unprovoked
shark attacks.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.625
Yeah, 80 unprovoked attacks.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.460
Or as President Trump
calls that, a weekend.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.129
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.462
-Yeah!

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:32.866
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.466
-Actually, Trump loves
"Shark Week."

00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:36.603
It's the one time he can tweet
"I love great whites"

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.205
without being called a racist.
[ Audience "oh"s ]

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.372
-Really?

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:45.545
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.715
-Speaking of the President,
the other day he invited

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.050
some reporters in to talk about
how he might put a tax

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.551
on French wine.

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:54.253
Even though he doesn't drink,
he still weighed in

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.589
on what he thinks about French
wine versus American wine.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.090
Listen to this.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.527
-I've always liked American
wines better than French wines.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.763
Even though I don't drink wine.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.598
I just like the way they look.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:09.669
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.070
-After that, his staffers
were like

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.238
everyone on "Family Feud"

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.773
after a teammate gives
a weird response.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.475
They're like, "Good answer.
Good --"

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.509
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:19.511
Show me
"Like the way they look"!

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:21.347
[ Imitates buzzer ]
Oh, sorry.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.683
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.184
It looks -- yeah.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.686
Some more political news.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.988
This week, there are two more
Democratic debates

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.523
and tomorrow's airs
at the same time

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.658
as "The Bachelorette" finale.
-Ooh.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:34.626
-So no matter which one
you watch,

00:01:34.626 --> 00:01:36.528
you'll see a bunch of sad guys
going home in a limo.

00:01:36.528 --> 00:01:37.730
It's just --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.064
No matter what.

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.566
But everyone's getting ready
for the next round

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:43.269
of Democratic debates, which are
this Tuesday and Wednesday.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.737
-Oh, man, that's great.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:48.574
I can't wait to see my favorite
candidate, Eric Swalwell.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.943
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.344
-You didn't hear, Tariq?

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:53.813
Eric Swalwell dropped out
of the race.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.647
He's actually the only candidate
not returning

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:57.049
to this round of debates.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.352
-Are you kidding me
right now?

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.220
-No, I'm -- I'm not kidding.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.422
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.757
You liked Eric Swalwell?
-Duh.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.826
Why else would I get
all these shirts made

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.494
that say "You can't --"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.563
"You can't spell 'America'
without 'Eric'"?

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.799
[ Laughter ]
-I had no idea that --

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:16.468
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:18.671
I had no idea that
you liked him so much.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.906
I -- I --

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.441
-I thought everyone did.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:25.278
Why else would I get
all these shirts made...

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.079
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.882
...that say "We don't need
a wall, we need a Swal"?

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.917
-Yeah, yeah -- Well, I --
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.720
I understand...

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.120
it must be upsetting,
but I'm sorry

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.522
I had to break it to you
like this.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.157
I mean...
-Man, this is the worst.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.227
Now what am I going to do
with all these shirts...

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.129
[ Laughter ]
...that say...

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.798
"All's swell that ends Swell"?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.566
-"All's well that's Swalwell"?

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.035
-Yeah, yeah, you know
what I mean.

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.904
-Well, these shirts are
getting worse and worse.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.538
Tariq, how many shirts
did you get made?

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.173
-I mean, who cares?
It doesn't matter anyway.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.476
I mean, who's even replacing him
in the debate?

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.144
-A guy named Steve Bullock.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.679
-Oh, man, really?
I love Steve Bullock.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:03.282
He was my second pick.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.051
-Please don't tell me
that you --

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.220
-Which is why I got all
these shirts made...

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.121
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:12.291
...that say, "Don't be fooled by
the rocks that I got.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.661
I'm still Steve from the --
Steve from the Bullock."

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:17.130
[ Laughter and applause ]
-All right, thank you very much.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.497
That's a pretty good one.
Thank you.

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:20.500
Tariq Trotter, everybody.
Tariq, thank you very much.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.836
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.504
[ Cheering continues ]

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.072
"I'm still Steve
from the Bullock."

00:03:27.072 --> 00:03:30.009
-Yeah. "From the Bullock."
"From the Bullock."

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.511
-"I'm still Steve
from the Bullock."

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.811
-Yeah.

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:35.881
And he's got a bunch of rocks.
-Some --

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.216
Some news from overseas.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.918
There are rumors that
Prince Harry and Meghan Markle

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.287
have banned their neighbors
from talking to them.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.522
-Ooh.
[ Audience "ooh"s ]

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.823
-Apparently the neighbors
aren't even allowed

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.157
to say "Good morning."
-Oh.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.525
-Right now you're thinking
that's rude,

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.061
but you're also
a little jealous.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.596
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.731
Check this out.
I heard that soon Teslas

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:55.334
will be able to stream Netflix
on the car's center display.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.004
It's all part of Tesla's plan
to cut down on emissions

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.338
and pedestrians.
-Oh.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:03.442
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:04.977
-Here's some good news
from Washington.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.714
Democrats and Republicans just
worked together to pass a bill

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.348
that would block robocalls.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:10.816
I think it's the one thing --

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:13.051
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.051 --> 00:04:14.653
It's the one thing
we can agree on,

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:16.489
that robocalls are the worst.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.225
-You know what, it's funny,
because I never get robocalls.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.793
-Well, you're one of
the lucky ones,

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.228
because they can be
pretty awful.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.562
[ Phone vibrating ]
-Oops, sorry.

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.965
Getting a phone call right now.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.900
That's weird.
It's my area code,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.768
but I don't recognize
the number.

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:31.437
-No, Higgins,
that is a robocall.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.138
-No, clearly it's a local call.

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:35.208
-No, no, Higgins, that's what
they do now. That's --

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.543
-Probably one of my relatives
from a random line

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.178
because their phone broke,
you know.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.680
-No, no, no. That's what
they want you to think.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.782
-No, no, no.
Here, I'll put it on speaker.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.483
You got the Steve.

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:48.453
-Hello, this is a call regarding
your computer's security.

00:04:48.453 --> 00:04:49.755
This is an emergency.

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.657
-Whoa, good thing I answered.
Huh, smart guy?

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:52.992
-No, no, no --
No, Higgins --

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.293
-You must update

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:57.096
your Social Security
information immediately.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:05:00.365
-Well, of course.
My Social Security is 9-8-7 --

00:05:00.365 --> 00:05:01.834
-No, no.
Higgins, Higgins, Higgins!

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.469
-This'll just take a second.
-No, don't --

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.304
It's 9 --
-Don't give them or America

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.140
your Social Security number
right now.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.641
That's crazy.
-Dude, it's totally cool.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.977
That's why they call it
"Social" Security.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.478
[ Laughter ]
It's meant to be social.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:13.813
It's meant to be shared.
-No, that's not --

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.114
That is not what it means,
actually.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.616
That's not what it --
-No, that's what it means.

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:18.250
No, you got a pen?
It's 9-8-7 --

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.552
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.821
-...6-5-4-3-2-6.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:24.022
And thank you for looking out
for me.

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:25.391
-I can't believe
you just did that.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.625
That -- it's a total scam.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.260
I mean, if you're not careful
with these calls,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.095
someone's going to steal
your identity.

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:31.764
-[ Laughs ]
Don't worry about it.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.765
Everything is fine.

00:05:33.765 --> 00:05:37.370
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.372
You just --
just do your monologue.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:45.745
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:49.015
[ Laughter continues ]

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:50.649
-What -- what are you
swiping?

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.552
-I'm on Tinder.
-Ah, get out of here.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.653
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:56.188
Oh, this isn't good here, guys.

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.257
A woman in Tennessee
was staying at a Hampton Inn

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.893
and she woke up when a snake
slithered across her body.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:01.994
[ Audience "ooh"s ]

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.395
Hampton Inn is defending
itself.

00:06:03.395 --> 00:06:05.030
They were like, "Well, did our
wake-up call work or not?"

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.398
I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:08.134
And finally, you guys,
I'm excited about this.

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.835
Tonight on the show
we have the winner

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:11.837
of the "Fortnite" World Cup
Championship...

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:15.241
[ Cheers and applause ]
...Kyle "Bugha" Giersdorf.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:19.244
He's just 16 years old
and he won $3 million.

00:06:19.244 --> 00:06:20.579
[ Cheers, gasping ]

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.414
Right now parents everywhere
are going, "All right,

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:24.183
put down your homework
and go play video games."

